# The programs the appliance's bless flow shells out to (DESIGN Section 7.5),
# staged with their library closure by mk-appliance.sh.
#
/usr/bin/sbsign          # signs the UKI wrap, and appends to a bare payload
/usr/bin/sbverify        # counts a payload's signatures before and after, one
                         # of the three checks that blessing ADDED ours and
                         # kept the vendor's (DESIGN Section 7.2)
# Neither cryptsetup nor bsdtar: p3 is opened and ISOs are read in process
# with falcon-core (falcon-appliance/src/shelf.c, the sign tool's isoview).
